WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.501
-Welcome back to the show,
everybody.

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:05.267
It is fall.

00:00:05.267 --> 00:00:07.167
The weather's
getting a little chilly.

00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:09.601
It's time to break out
the hats and gloves.

00:00:09.601 --> 00:00:11.100
And with that in mind,
it's time to play the game

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:12.267
that's sweeping the nation.

00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:16.067
It's time for
"Dance Your Hat and Gloves Off."

00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:21.067
-♪ "Dance Your Hat
and Gloves Off ♪

00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:22.934
♪ Come on and dance 'em off ♪

00:00:22.934 --> 00:00:24.801
-Welcome to
"Dance Your Hat and Gloves Off."

00:00:24.801 --> 00:00:26.567
Release the mirror ball!

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:29.200
There you go. This...

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:30.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:36.234
This is the game where we put
hats and gloves on people

00:00:36.234 --> 00:00:38.133
and make them dance
until they fall off.

00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:41.267
Now let's meet our contestants.
Come on over, everybody!

00:00:41.267 --> 00:00:44.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.434
Looking good.

00:00:45.434 --> 00:00:47.467
Looking good
in the neighborhood.

00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:48.801
What is your name
and where are you from?

00:00:48.801 --> 00:00:50.667
-Spencer Jones
from Tyler, Texas.

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:52.834
-Hey! Tyler, Texas.

00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:53.934
Spencer,
thank you for being here.

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:55.133
What's your name?
Where are you from?

00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:56.767
-Nadiah Malik.
Freehold, new Jersey.

00:00:56.767 --> 00:00:59.501
-Oh, yeah!
-Whoo!

00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:00.834
-Guest number three.

00:01:00.834 --> 00:01:02.367
-Davis Roper.
Raleigh, North Carolina.

00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:06.400
-Oh, wow! Davis, Raleigh.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.067
Now, are you guys
ready to do this?

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:09.133
-We're ready.
-Here you go.

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:10.534
Here's how the game works.

00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:12.834
One at a time, you'll take
your place on the dance floor.

00:01:12.834 --> 00:01:16.767
Don't be worried about that
mirrorball. It will not fall.

00:01:16.767 --> 00:01:18.834
It hasn't yet. It hasn't yet.

00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:21.534
But when I say "dance,"
you're going to have 15 seconds

00:01:21.534 --> 00:01:23.167
to fling your hat
and gloves off.

00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:25.901
Scoring is simple -- 1 point
for each glove you get off,

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:27.200
2 points for the hat.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:29.434
Whoever gets the most points
wins the grand prize.

00:01:29.434 --> 00:01:31.968
And, oh, what a prize it is.
Higgins?

00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:33.834
-Well, Jimmy, tonight's winner
will be taking home

00:01:33.834 --> 00:01:35.601
a treasure map
that shows the precise

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:39.100
location of three $100 bills
that are vacuum-sealed

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:41.567
and floating in the middle
of the Atlantic Ocean.

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:43.667
Jimmy?

00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:47.033
-Yeah!
-Thank you. Higgins.

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:48.100
Thank you, Higgins.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.234
What would you do
with that $300, Higgins?

00:01:50.234 --> 00:01:51.934
-Wow. Thanks for asking.

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:53.901
You know, my son's been needing

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:55.467
a little money --
needs some dental work done.

00:01:55.467 --> 00:01:57.601
And I was hoping to take
that $300 and --

00:01:57.601 --> 00:01:58.868
-A couple of things
before we start.

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:01.400
At no time can you touch
the hat or gloves,

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:02.767
nor can anything touch them.

00:02:02.767 --> 00:02:05.133
Basically, you just have to whip
your arms and head around

00:02:05.133 --> 00:02:07.667
as crazy as you can
until everything falls off.

00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:10.067
In the event of a tie,
our audience will decide

00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:12.334
the winner
based on your dancing skills.

00:02:12.334 --> 00:02:15.200
So bring it.
You ready for this?

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.300
-We're ready.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:19.234
-Alright, buddy,
you are up first.

00:02:19.234 --> 00:02:20.801
Audience, let's cheer him on.

00:02:20.801 --> 00:02:23.634
You can hit the dance star
right there.

00:02:23.634 --> 00:02:25.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:02:25.934 --> 00:02:28.267
Alright. Ready...

00:02:28.267 --> 00:02:30.601
set...dance!

00:02:30.601 --> 00:02:33.167
Yeah. That's it. Yeah.

00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:34.300
Yeah, yeah. Yeah.

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:37.400
Yeah.

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:40.367
Yeah! Come on! Go!

00:02:40.367 --> 00:02:42.667
Come on!
Unh! Unh! Unh! Unh!

00:02:42.667 --> 00:02:44.634
Come on! Yeah! Unh! Go!

00:02:44.634 --> 00:02:46.234
Come on! Yeah! Yeah!

00:02:46.234 --> 00:02:48.634
[ Dinging ]

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:50.667
That's it.

00:02:50.667 --> 00:02:55.000
Oh, nice try. Nice job.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.467
It's harder than it looks.
It's harder than it looks.

00:02:57.467 --> 00:02:59.501
It's much easier at home, when
you're playing the home game.

00:02:59.501 --> 00:03:02.367
-That's true.
-Yeah. But that was fantastic.

00:03:02.367 --> 00:03:03.767
Can we see what you did
in slow motion

00:03:03.767 --> 00:03:05.167
so you can see, as well?

00:03:05.167 --> 00:03:06.901
That's what you basically did.

00:03:06.901 --> 00:03:08.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:10.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah, fanta--

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.801
[ Laughs ]
That's fantastic.

00:03:12.801 --> 00:03:14.434
Is that how you dance
at weddings, as well?

00:03:14.434 --> 00:03:16.467
-I do.
-Yeah, that's right. Well done.

00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:18.601
Higgins, how many points?

00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:21.634
Ooh! Alright. There you go.
That's right.

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:24.567
Hey, if everyone gets zero,
you still get a good chance.

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:27.200
That was a good style.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:28.434
Contestant number two,
you are up,

00:03:28.434 --> 00:03:29.934
so why don't you hit
the dance spot

00:03:29.934 --> 00:03:30.934
whenever you're ready to go.

00:03:30.934 --> 00:03:32.868
Audience, cheer her on, please.

00:03:32.868 --> 00:03:34.434
Ready...

00:03:34.434 --> 00:03:36.701
set...dance!

00:03:36.701 --> 00:03:38.501
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:03:38.501 --> 00:03:40.834
Oh, yeah! Oh, yeah!
That's 2 points! Yes!

00:03:40.834 --> 00:03:43.267
Go, go! Hey, go!

00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:44.367
Oh!
[ Dinging ]

00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:47.501
That's fantastic! Unbelievable!

00:03:47.501 --> 00:03:49.968
Unbelievable! Wow!

00:03:49.968 --> 00:03:51.534
That is fant--
Come on over here.

00:03:51.534 --> 00:03:53.667
That is definitely
unbelievable moves.

00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:54.801
You are in the lead.

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:57.534
Can we see that
in slow motion, please?

00:03:57.534 --> 00:04:00.934
Look at this.
Hat came right off.

00:04:00.934 --> 00:04:02.734
And then --
Yeah, and then -- What?

00:04:02.734 --> 00:04:03.734
You felt it right there.

00:04:03.734 --> 00:04:07.667
One, two, three,
bam, right there!

00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:12.467
Fantastic job.
Higgins, how many points?

00:04:12.467 --> 00:04:15.601
Ooh, ooh, wow.
Oh, there you go!

00:04:15.601 --> 00:04:18.634
It's a perfect score.
Perfect score.

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:19.801
But you know what that means.

00:04:19.801 --> 00:04:21.334
We're down to our
last contestant here.

00:04:21.334 --> 00:04:24.334
Now, you got to show up.
-A lot of pressure.

00:04:24.334 --> 00:04:26.000
-Yeah, over in
Raleigh, North Carolina,

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:27.701
do they do some wild dancing?

00:04:27.701 --> 00:04:29.267
-You know it.
Better than anywhere else.

00:04:29.267 --> 00:04:32.868
-Now, you're happy with
your glasses remaining on?

00:04:32.868 --> 00:04:35.434
-We'll find out.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.434 --> 00:04:37.133
-I like this. I like this.

00:04:37.133 --> 00:04:40.067
I kind of want to see them
fly off a little bit, yeah.

00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:41.434
-Me too, me too.

00:04:41.434 --> 00:04:43.567
-That 300 bucks, if you find it
in the Atlantic Ocean,

00:04:43.567 --> 00:04:44.901
could pay for new frames.

00:04:44.901 --> 00:04:46.601
-Worth it, worth it.
-Yeah, it is so worth it.

00:04:46.601 --> 00:04:47.767
Alright, why don't you
go over here,

00:04:47.767 --> 00:04:49.100
and whenever you're ready --

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:50.934
I'll move these out of
the way here so you don't...

00:04:50.934 --> 00:04:53.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:53.467 --> 00:04:56.400
I want to make sure
you're in the clear.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:58.000
You're okay? You're ready to go?
-I'm ready. I'm ready.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:01.133
-Okay, audience,
put your hands together.

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:04.200
Ready, set...dance!

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:05.601
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:05:05.601 --> 00:05:07.300
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah!

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:09.434
Whoa, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh!

00:05:09.434 --> 00:05:11.868
Yes!
[ Dinging ]

00:05:11.868 --> 00:05:13.901
That -- Wow!

00:05:13.901 --> 00:05:17.901
That was fantastic!
Oh, my gosh!

00:05:17.901 --> 00:05:19.901
That's never happened

00:05:19.901 --> 00:05:21.634
in the history of
"Dance Your Hat and --"

00:05:21.634 --> 00:05:23.267
You feel like...
-Yeah.

00:05:23.267 --> 00:05:24.467
-Yeah, I know, I know.

00:05:24.467 --> 00:05:25.834
Don't even tell me.
Don't even tell me.

00:05:25.834 --> 00:05:28.901
Let's see what you did
in slow motion.

00:05:28.901 --> 00:05:31.167
Look at this.
Yeah. One, two.

00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:32.767
Get that other one off.
You're focused.

00:05:32.767 --> 00:05:36.701
Yes! You felt the headbang,
and the glasses stayed on.

00:05:36.701 --> 00:05:39.501
Then now look at this. Yes!

00:05:39.501 --> 00:05:42.133
Yes! That was like...

00:05:42.133 --> 00:05:44.067
That was well done.

00:05:44.067 --> 00:05:46.634
Higgins, how many points
did he get there?

00:05:47.467 --> 00:05:50.000
That's it right there -- 4.
That's not bad.

00:05:51.667 --> 00:05:55.767
But that means our audience
has to decide the winner.

00:05:55.767 --> 00:05:57.601
Yeah.

00:05:57.601 --> 00:05:59.067
You can have a seat,
if you'd like.

00:05:59.067 --> 00:06:00.200
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:02.033
That's right.
Yeah. No. No, please.

00:06:02.033 --> 00:06:04.901
Is it contestant number two?

00:06:04.901 --> 00:06:06.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:08.767 --> 00:06:11.534
Or is it contestant
number three?

00:06:11.534 --> 00:06:13.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah!

00:06:13.801 --> 00:06:15.501
-Contestant number
three is the winner!

00:06:15.501 --> 00:06:16.734
Congratulations!

00:06:16.734 --> 00:06:18.534
Here is your treasure map

00:06:18.534 --> 00:06:21.234
